      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Upon transitioning to a decentralized model with 50 localized nodes over the next 90 days, you can expect a certain degree of initial disruption. Quantifying this, expertise in past transitions suggests that there may be a 10-30% increase in average delivery timelines, depending on various factors like regional preparedness and the robustness of local node implementations.\n\nRisks during this 90-day period potentially include:\n\n1. Node Overload: As nodes are not accustomed to the central task flow, they could experience bottlenecks during peak times, further delaying medication delivery. Anticipate a starting delay of a few hours to potentially up to 48 hours, escalating until the decentralized system fully operates.\n\n2. Inconsistent Capabilities: Different regional nodes have diverse infrastructure and resources; this may lead to significant disparities in efficiency, whereby some may struggle with processing or real-time tracking, resulting in unexplained medication backups or early dispatches.\n\n3. Security Vulnerability: An expanded attack surface area with 50 nodes increases the risk of cyberattacks. Expect data breaches in the initial phase, which could necessitate pausing other operations to address and rectify the security concerns.\n\n4. Staff Unfamiliarity: Your staff may experience a learning curve; frustration and mistakes",
      "source": "target",
